module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_text_actual_at_a_free_monoid_run_carrier_is_unjudged

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// A TEXT ACTUAL REACHING A FREE-MONOID CARRIER IS NOT A KERNEL VALUE AT A STRUCTURED HEAD, AND THE
// CAST ROW ITSELF SAYS SO. The family's first repair (#12398) refused the SCALAR at a declared
// element collection -- `list_at_index(xs: List<String>, index: 1)`, `take(xs: FreeMonoid<Int>)`
// handed an Int -- and its predicate is `is_kernel_type(actual) && !node_is_element_collection(declared)`.
// This pair does not fit it: the actual is TEXT and the carrier is the free-monoid ALGEBRA spelling.
// std.coercion's grounded identity carriers list `String -> FreeMonoid` (operator Ruling 3,
// 2026-07-15: "a String IS a FreeMonoid<Char>"; dag/std/types.dag:159 declares `type String =
// FreeMonoid<Char>`) -- the identity is real, and it is a run OVER CHAR. The function that could
// have refused, `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded`, ABSTAINS exactly because a cast row
// reaches the pair: its own doc is explicit that a cast row elsewhere does not license an
// inhabitance verdict HERE and that it answers `none` when its shape test fails. So nothing judged
// the pair, and the relation answered its counted InhabitanceUnmodeled default: the wall counts the
// abstention loudly and changes no verdict, and the program runs.
//
// WHY THE ARM ALONE WAS NOT ENOUGH, MEASURED. The refusal needs the demanded element GROUNDED; the
// call's own unification is what grounds it, and it does not for this pair. An Int at a CONCRETE
// `FreeMonoid<String>` formal refuses (`declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>)', produced
// 'Primitive(Int)'`), while the same Int at `FreeMonoid<T>` with a sibling argument of `List<String>`
// that settles T says NOTHING at that argument -- the element never reaches the argument obligation.
// The descent in `unify_generics` pairs children positionally only when the two sides share a
// CONNECTIVE, which is a property of the form each side arrives in, not of the carrier: one carrier
// under two spellings (std.algebra's roster declares FreeMonoid as the algebra and List as its
// container alias, `carrier_spellings` rows carrying `container_algebra_row` and
// `container_alias_row`, `canonical_template_name` mapping both to one template name) bound nothing.
// A refusal built from a sibling argument's element is the fabricated verdict review 97406 named, so
// the grounding had to move UP to where the binding is made, and stay narrow: children are the
// coproduct's VARIANTS when a list element arrives through its declaration, and pairing them against
// an application is exactly the accident gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge records (R bound to
// the variant `StepEstablished`, every arm of a match over the receipt then refused: `variant not
// found in type StepOutcome`). So the branch fires only when both sides are registered element
// collections (`node_is_element_collection`) whose canonical template names agree.
//
// WHY THAT IS NOT A NON-BUG: the run answers. std.algebra's `list_append(left: ["a"], right: "bc")`
// -- an element where a run is required, the `list_push`/`list_append` mix-up authors make --
// evaluated to ["a", "bc"] (PR #16535 side chat finding F2), because the interpreter's list-concat
// arm `match right { Node(FreeMonoid...) => ..., __ => [head, *tail] }` pushes whatever is not a
// carrier as one item (v1.compiler.interpreter). The guarantee is the whole point of this frontier:
// a value of one declared type reaches a position declaring another, and the compiler carries no
// verdict, so the program runs and answers -- and the answer is plausible. The ceiling is
// ordinary: the compiler refuses wrong-shape arguments as a matter of course everywhere else in
// this family; the missing part is the judgment, not the ability to express it.
data a_text_actual_at_a_free_monoid_run_carrier_is_unjudged: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_text_actual_at_a_free_monoid_run_carrier_is_unjudged" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "BOUNDED, AND IT NAMES ITS OWN DISSOLUTION, because an unbounded trigger turns a filed hole into infrastructure the next reader cannot tell from a guarantee. THIS ROW IS CLOSED BY THE JUDGMENT, NOT BY A REWRITING OF SUBSTITUTION: the located refusal arm `text_actual_at_run_of_non_char_element` (v1.compiler.infer, reached from `run_element_demand`) fires on DECLARATION IDENTITY -- the actual is text, the formal's type is the FreeMonoid declaration, and the element type is settled and is not Char -- with the element question answered by the single existing authority v1.compiler.infer_env::text_element_is_char rather than a new reader. Where the call settles the element (a bare formal, a concrete carrier, or the call's own unification) the site refuses at typecheck naming argument and parameter, and the ticket's own `list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\")` is the witnessed instance. THE REMAINING BOUND IS THE UNSETTLED ELEMENT, AND IT IS THE ONLY ONE: when the element cannot be settled from the call the arm answers TextRepresentationUnidentified and fabricates no verdict -- the fail_closed answer (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed: no plausible output is fabricated), not a refusal. THAT IS THE ONE EVENT THIS ROW STILL WAITS ON, and it is a HYPOTHESIS POINTING AT ANOTHER ROW'S FIRST_SLICE, not a cause this row owns or asserts: `generic-substitution-skips-the-subtree-under-a-type-variable-inferred-node` (rn_3PJTV4JA4RY3IRWQ2POQOPFEZK, NotDispatchable, carriers src/v1/04_infer.dag + src/v1/04_env.dag, rostered by plan PR #17098) asks what leaves an element unsettled and points at v1.compiler.infer::substitute_generics_apply (src/v1/04_infer.dag:18654). TWO OF THAT ROW'S CLAIMS ARE WITHDRAWN, and they are recorded here so no reader re-takes them. (1) A KEY SPLIT between the map's key domain and the TypeVariable id domain: WRONG. unify_generics (src/v1/04_infer.dag:18434) inserts `map_insert(acc, bind_name, actual)` at :18441 and :18457 keyed by the generic's NAME, and TypeVariable ids are minted FROM that same name (src/v1/04_env.dag:1268 `TypeVariable { id: name }`; src/v1/04_infer.dag:19793 `TypeVariable { id: nm }`), so the two domains agree. (2) THAT ARM 1 SKIPS THE SUBTREE under a TypeVariable-inferred node: UNSUPPORTED BY MEASUREMENT. Arm 1 (:18656-18660) does return on both outcomes -- hit at :18658, silent `Absent => n` at :18659 -- and the body's only three recursive calls sit in arm 2 (:18671 children, :18672 params, :18675 the Resolved inferred); but a scratch-only instrument over the whole emitted population measured applications=16508, nodes_visited=82143, arm1=19681, hit=19021, silent_miss=660, and swallowed subtree nodes = 0 (2026-11-25 at head 720683bdb063; the counters lived in a copied tree and the shipped binary carries no counter). WHAT SURVIVES IS A TYPED HAZARD WITH A BOUNDED TRIGGER, not an accepted hole and not this row's obligation: arm 1 returns without entering children at 19681 nodes, 660 of them on the silent miss; and the deferred-field-access sentinel minter that motivated the story (src/v1/04_infer.dag:11476-11484, gate :11474-11475 `is_deferred_field_access_base && !is_never_constrained_enclosing_generic_base`) is ORDINARY rather than rare -- both halves of that gate are true at 8 sites, 5 in src/v2/compiler/tokenize.dag and 3 in src/v2/std/text.dag, all under the tokenize entry and zero elsewhere. The repair direction the split decides (19021 hits against 660 misses, 96.65% / 3.35%) is to recurse into the SUBSTITUTED node's children after a HIT, not to fall through to arm 2. THE INSTRUMENT'S OWN BLIND SPOT, named by the one who built it: its wrapper early-returns on an empty substitution map WITHOUT emitting a record, so an empty-map arrival is invisible -- an absence you cannot see through is not an absence, and SWALLOW=0 must be re-measured with that gap closed before anyone retires the other row on it. THE FIVE SIBLING ROWS that name substitute_generics_apply as their own site -- error_type_fabricated_as_a_type_by_total_accessors, field_access_on_a_generic_call_result_keeps_the_uninstantiated_parameter, generic_identity_decided_by_spelling, generic_optional_over_a_type_application_argument_loses_the_optional, silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics -- are that row's census to explain; measured 2026-11-25 at origin/main d54195db4478 by `git grep -l substitute_generics_apply origin/main -- dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/*.dag`, which named exactly those five before #17098 landed. UNTIL THE UNSETTLED-ELEMENT ARM EXISTS THE WALL IS NOT THE GUARANTEE: it refuses where the call settles the element and says nothing where the call cannot. A reader who finds this row with the refusal arm present and the unsettled-element arm absent is looking at the bound, not at the ticket." } },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: raw lines, the main tip it was taken at, the released claim_batch's sha256 and the process's real exit status are recorded in the PR #16894 evidence comment, section 'RED on main'",
    "MECHANISM: the pair reaches neither an arm nor the kernel-mismatch function, because the cast row String -> FreeMonoid makes that function abstain by design (its doc: a cast row elsewhere does not license an inhabitance verdict here; it answers none when its shape test fails). The relation therefore answers InhabitanceUnmodeled, which the wall counts and does not act on, and v1.compiler.interpreter list-concat `match right { Node(FreeMonoid...) => ..., __ => [head, *tail] }` pushes the non-carrier as one item, so the program RUNS and answers a plausible list.",
    "NON-VACUITY CONTROLS: the two-sided table in the PR #16894 evidence comment (section 'CONTROLS'): `list_append` over two runs and `list_push` over a run and an element stay accepted alongside the refusals, so the rule is not a ban on the carrier",
    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: this does not mean the program's value is wrong, nor that text at a run over Char is refused -- that IS std.coercion's identity, and its rows stay green (`list_append(left: \"ab\", right: \"bc\")`, and `take(xs: FreeMonoid<Char>)` handed text, green in the two-sided table of the PR #16894 evidence comment (section 'GREEN at head') and in test.claim.declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_witness). Grounding is not asserted here: it is measured, by the refusal of `text_at_a_declared_run_of_int_is_refused` (a run-of-Int carrier with a grounded element, refused) read against the silence of the two controls whose element the call never settles",
    "RELATION TO THE ROWS THAT ALREADY OWN PART OF THIS CHAIN: a_primitive_actual_at_a_declared_container_is_unjudged (PR #12398) closed the SCALAR-at-carrier pair -- Int at List<String>, Int at FreeMonoid<T> -- and a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only (PR #12398) holds the both-containers-arguments-disagree pair. This row is the pair NEITHER covers: a text actual at the ALGEBRA spelling of a carrier, which the earlier predicate `is_kernel_type(actual) && !node_is_element_collection(declared)` cannot reach because the cast row that makes text a legitimate carrier value is exactly what the refusal predicate abstains on. The fix is therefore a new arm in the relation, not a widening of that predicate.",
        "FIX (PR #16894): two changes at the one seam each owns, plus the same witness on both sides. In src/v1/04_infer.dag: (i) `declared_type_inhabitance` gains its last judgment before the terminal InhabitanceUnmodeled abstention -- a new reason variant RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement refusing a TEXT actual at the run carrier when the demanded element is grounded and is not the declared Char. All three sides are decided by DECLARATION, never by spelling (review 97588; gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate): the actual through text_representation_by_identity, which keeps the kernel String mint apart from the corpus run-of-Char and from v2.std.text.String (gunbc.design_ruling::text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold); the carrier and the element through v1's one type-reference derivation, compared as DeclarationRefs against the canonical refs the text wall already names -- text_identity_std_algebra_free_monoid -- so a module-local 'type Char' does not inherit the identity and an alias of the carrier is the carrier; the element itself is answered by `run_element_demand` and nothing else, since text is licensed at a run position only OVER the declared Char and the wall asks no brand authority whether Char widens to the declared element (the crossing changes interpretation, so gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate declines it: 'Bool does not implicitly inhabit Int'), reusing the located DeclaredTypeNotInhabited census key so the refusal names the parameter and renders both types, with no new solver and no re-derivation (tidy-ant-251); (ii) `unify_generics` grounds the element where the call's own map is built, descending children only for a pair of registered element collections whose canonical template name agrees. the regenerated mirror committed at the head the GREEN table was produced from, and the required regen round ending green on that head; (iii) the one seed site that needed the crossing pays for it explicitly -- `std.source_annotation.advance_line_prefix_indent_only_text` maps its code points through `std.unicode.char_class.unicode_char_code_point` rather than pouring a run of Int into a run of Char -- which is why no call site depends on the implicit direction, with the new module's row in src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag beside 'std_unicode_scalar' in the unit that already holds 'std_source_annotation' and a declared edge between them (intra-crate, so it cannot trip Stage0EmittedEdgesRefused) -- receipts in the PR #16894 evidence comment (section 'GREEN at head')",
    "THE GUARD, MEASURED, AND WHY THE RULE MAY NOT REFUSE AN UNSETTLED ELEMENT: the first head of this PR passed its own witness and still failed the population. The heal round (heal-generated-artifacts, run 45201706042, job 137786624164, head 099ab008e3) refused the next generation with eleven errors main does not produce, all in src/v2/std/text.dag -- `is_empty(xs: s)`, `for_all(xs: s, predicate: fn(c) { ... })`, `list_append(left: acc, right: field)` over two Strings -- each reading `declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)', produced 'Node(String<Product(Char)>)'` under this rule's own key. The declared side names the defect: `Primitive()` is an element the call never settled. `direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags` hands the obligation the unsolved `substitution_basis` wherever `direct_call_formal_has_unbound_type_variable` still holds, and a rule that asks only `settled(element) && element != Char` reads an empty slot as a declaration that is not Char and refuses the standard library. The arm now asks the seam's own question of the element -- `direct_call_formal_has_unbound_type_variable` of the element argument -- and answers nothing while it is unsettled or settling to the empty placeholder: `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` asks for a located diagnostic where a verdict EXISTS and silence where none does, never a verdict invented from a slot. Two zero-row controls in the witness hold the corpus shapes: text_at_a_run_whose_element_the_call_never_settles_is_no_verdict and text_at_a_run_whose_element_a_lambda_settles_is_no_verdict. the whole-population differential in the PR #16894 evidence comment (section 'POPULATION'): two binaries over the same tree, the newly-refused set empty, with the line counts of both sides printed so an empty set is a measured empty",
    "MEASURED OVER-REFUSALS OF THIS CLASS, BOTH FOUND ONLY BY THE POPULATION (the witness stayed green both times). READING 1: keyed on the element read from the ACTUAL's stamped declaration, the arm refused eleven src/v2/std/text.dag call sites (`declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)', produced 'Node(String<Product(Char)>)'`), the failure surfacing as a heal round refusing the next generation rather than as a red claim. READING 2: keyed on `the settled element is not Char` alone, the arm refused ONE correct std call that the seed's own lattice licenses -- `dag/std/source_annotation.dag`'s `advance_line_prefix_indent_only_text` feeding `unicode_scalar_unfold (s: String) -> FreeMonoid<Char>` into a `code_points: List<Int>` folded by `code_point_is_line_feed(cp: Int)`, S2B_REGEN_REAL_EXIT=1 with a single hard diagnostic. `std.types.Char` is `type Char = Int where unicode_scalar, brand("Char")` (dag/std/types.dag:158) and this file's own `brand_grounds_transparently_to` -- consulted in both directions by `nominal_call_arg_brand_mismatch` -- says a brand grounds transparently to what it brands. The repair is to ASK THAT AUTHORITY on the element pair and adopt its answer (no second brand test), and separately to make the call site bridge element-wise through `unicode_char_code_point` (`c + 0`, dag/std/unicode/char_class.dag:10) exactly as dag/std/annotation_reference.dag:123 does.",

    "MEASURED INERTNESS OF THIS CLASS, THE COSTLIER READING. The arm was written, typechecked, passed review and NEVER FIRED for three iterations: the table stayed bit-identical across three materially different heads. Two static reasons, both measured: `declared_is_generic` (params > 0 OR the inferred is a TypeVariable) consumes every `FreeMonoid<alias>` pair before a judgment placed after it can see it, and after hoisting, the element child the call-substituted formal carries is a KERNEL CONNECTIVE (`Primitive(String)`, `Primitive(Int)`, empty `Primitive()`), which carries no declaration -- so `type_reference_declaration_reading` answers TypeReferenceIsKernelType and `settled_type` answers none, and both readers abstain in every placement. A reachable arm and an inert arm look identical from a green witness. PROOF OF REACHABILITY IS THE OBSERVED VERDICT MOVING, not the code being present: read the emitted Rust's call order, and refuse to call a table green when it did not change.",

    "THE BASELINE OBSERVATION, WITH ITS RECEIPTS (the receipts live HERE, not in the code comments that cite the class). Taken on a main tree at head b69155949654 with that head's RELEASED claim_batch (release-bins artifact, sha256 632e3c6a...), on srv1 under the shared heavy limiter, three source roots, entry closure only: (1) an Int at a CONCRETE `FreeMonoid<String>` formal REFUSES -- `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'x', declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>)', produced 'Primitive(Int)'`; (2) the same Int at a GENERIC `FreeMonoid<T>` formal whose element the call settles through a sibling run of String says NOTHING AT ALL: `two_fm<T>(left: FreeMonoid<T>, right: FreeMonoid<T>)` called `two_fm(left: ["a"], right: 1)` yields no diagnostic and no obligation -- the obligation is handed a carrier with no element, so the arms of the family have nothing to compare and the pair runs; (3) the ticket's repro `list_append(left: ["a"], right: "bc")` compiled with ZERO refusals and evaluated to the plausible `["a", "bc"]`. Counted inertness of the same class: the first three placements of this arm each produced a witness table BIT-IDENTICAL to main (17 rows, unchanged) while the arm was typechecked and present -- `observed 0` refusals on every must-refuse row, three times over, which is the run that must be read as a failure and not as a green. raw lines, the main tip it was taken at, the released claim_batch's sha256 and the process's real exit status are recorded in the PR #16894 evidence comment, section 'RED on main'",
    "THE LICENSING THAT WAS REMOVED, AND ON WHAT AUTHORITY (2026-11-24). The first heads of the wall put the element pair to `brand_grounds_transparently_to` -- the same authority `nominal_call_arg_brand_mismatch` consults at a call argument -- and on a yes (Char, a branded refinement of Int, grounding transparently to Int) they ABSTAINED, so text at a declared run of Int compiled. That is an implicit coercion across a change of interpretation: a run of Char read as a run of code-point Ints. gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate already refuses exactly that kind of coercion ('Bool does not implicitly inhabit Int'), so the licensing is removed and NO gunbc.design_ruling row is minted -- the authority is the existing argument, not a person, and a ruling row asserting a decision nobody recorded would be worse than none. Consequence to expect when reading the population: text at a `FreeMonoid<Int>` position is now refused, and the only admitted way to write it is element-wise through the module named in the FIX field. The lane's boundary on this: if the whole-population newly-refused census shows ANY site beyond this PR's own fixtures, that is a corpus-wide behaviour change and it stops at the lane manager, who takes it to the operator with Hold as the default; the census prints site identity (module path and line) for exactly that reason. THIS ROW DOES NOT CLOSE gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.char_brand_admits_any_int: that row is on main with rung RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated } and stays open -- it is the confinement class (the brand admitting any Int at a CHAR position, measured by gunbc run at the value level on 2026-10-05), a different class from this one, which judges a run CARRIER's element. None of its measurement legs is made stale by removing this licensing: it measures char_text resolutions, and this change adds a refusal at an argument position. That the confinement class remains open is the honest ceiling statement here, not an oversight of this row.",
    "WHAT THE POPULATION CLAIM RESTS ON: s13 alone -- the whole-population newly-refused census, main's binary against the head's over the same tree. Two planned legs were DROPPED BY LANE-MANAGER RULING (2026-11-24), not by oversight, and the next worker should not re-plan them: a neighbour-corpus run (s7) and a reachable-population run (s8c), each of which would answer a weaker version of the same question at the cost of a slot the node does not have. The ruling's words: the s13 newly-refused set dominates both.",
    "THE KEY THE WITNESS ACTUALLY JOINS ON, so the next reader does not invent a fourth spelling: the census row's `diagnostic_class` is `DeclaredTypeNotInhabited` — taken from the DIAGNOSTIC KIND, not from the refusal reason — narrowed to rows whose `subject_name` contains the parameter name the fixture itself declares, in single quotes. The refusal's own identity is the reason variant `InhabitanceRefused { reason: RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement }`, emitted at `position: PositionDirectCallArgument` with `subject: app.formal.parameter_identity` (src/v1/04_infer.dag:7961-7980) and rendered by `v1.compiler.infer::inhabitance_refusal_position_label`. A claim CANNOT import that renderer (layer fact, not an oversight: the witness roots are dag + src/v2 per gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots::witness_layer_roots, while `v1.compiler.infer` is declared under src/v1), which is exactly why the join is class AND subject_name and why no prose of the label is stored in the witness to go stale when the prose is reworded.",
    "MEASURED REACHABILITY AND THE SIX VICTIM SITES THE WALL NEWLY REFUSED IN THIS PR'S OWN BUILD (run 45575541152, job `emit and build //gunbc/instruments:self-host`, `floor_class=structural exit=2`): six diagnostics, one per site, each reading `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'code_points' [RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement: a text value inhabits a FreeMonoid carrier only as a run over Char (std.coercion's grounded identity carrier String -> FreeMonoid); the carrier's declared element is not Char, so the text does not inhabit it]: declared 'Container(List,Primitive(Int))', produced 'Node(std.algebra.FreeMonoid<Product(Char)>)'` at src/v2/compiler/tokenize.dag:1128:126, 1129:95, 1185:126, 1186:95, 1249:118, 1250:87. The v2 lexer's lexeme is a v2.std.text.String, which is std.algebra.FreeMonoid<Char> (src/v2/std/text.dag:7), so those six sites reached a code-point parameter only through the hole this row files; they now feed the shared rules through ONE module-local bridge, `lexeme_code_points` at src/v2/compiler/tokenize.dag:863, a named conversion and never a cast (gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate). THIS RECEIPT IS ARM REACHABILITY PROVED BY THE PR'S OWN BUILD, NOT WITNESS EXECUTION: gunbc CI executes no claims, no claim row of any kind was executed there, and no local emit-route leg was possible at this head because NO arm-bearing `gunbc` binary existed anywhere in the workspace. The ACCEPTANCE half is proved by the same build: dag/std/source_annotation.dag:110 passes exactly the bridge's argument shape — `list_map(xs: unicode_scalar_unfold(s: lexeme), f: fn(c) { unicode_char_code_point(c: c) })`, a FreeMonoid<Int> — into `code_points: List<Int>` under the same wall-bearing binary, and that run emitted SIX diagnostics at src/v2/compiler/tokenize.dag and ZERO at dag/std/source_annotation.dag (diagnostics counted by file in that log: 6 and 0). The wall has already seen that argument shape and did not refuse it.",
    "THE MEASURED REASON THE SILENT SITES ARE SILENT, and why the repair may not be built at a consumer. WRITE SIDE, CORRECTED 2026-11-25 after reading main's bytes end to end. An earlier version of this row described a TWO-DOMAIN KEY SPLIT, with the writer at src/v1/04_infer.dag:18660/:18666 and the reader at :18882-18887; those citations are WRONG and the story was never the defect -- :18660 and :18666 sit inside the READER's own first arm, and :18882-18887 is a TypeEnv ancestry rebuild in a different function. What the bytes say: `unify_generics` (:18434) is the substitution map's ONLY writer and it writes ONE key domain, `map_insert(acc, bind_name, actual)` at :18441 and :18457 keyed by the generic's NAME; that map is the argument fold's `st.subst` (:10731, threaded at :10795), reaching the plan as `let call_subst = arg_call.subst` (:11837), which is what the obligation's declared type is built with (`substitute_generics(n: carried.declared_type, subst: call_subst, source_indices: source_indices)` at :7797). READ SIDE: `substitute_generics_apply` (:18654) dispatches FIRST on `n.inferred`, and its arms are not symmetric -- arm 1 (:18656-18660) matches `Present { value: TypeVariable { id: tv_id } }`, asks the map for that id, and RETURNS ON BOTH OUTCOMES (hit :18658, silent `Absent => n` at :18659 with no diagnostic), while the only three recursive calls in the body are inside arm 2 (:18671 children, :18672 params, :18675 the Resolved inferred). So any node whose inferred is a TypeVariable has its children, its params and its inferred subtree skipped by substitution ENTIRELY, hit or miss: an un-entered subtree, not a key mismatch. TypeVariable ids are minted FROM names (src/v1/04_env.dag:1268 `TypeVariable { id: name }`; src/v1/04_infer.dag:19793 `TypeVariable { id: nm }`), which is why the domains usually agree -- and the ONE minter that does not use a name is what bites: the deferred-field-access path at src/v1/04_infer.dag:11476-11484 builds `make_named_expr_node(... children: [base_typed], inferred: Present { value: TypeVariable { id: \"field_of_type_var\" } })`, a node carrying CHILDREN under a synthetic sentinel id that can never equal a generic name, gated by `is_deferred_field_access_base && !is_never_constrained_enclosing_generic_base` at :11474-11475. That is exactly the shape this wall's silent repro reaches: a formal that is a deferred field access on a type-variable base, whose child keeps its unsubstituted spelling. THE REPAIR NOW HAS AN OWNING ROW, and it is NOT this one: plan PR #17098 rostered `generic-substitution-skips-the-subtree-under-a-type-variable-inferred-node` (identity rn_3PJTV4JA4RY3IRWQ2POQOPFEZK, carriers src/v1/04_infer.dag + src/v1/04_env.dag, NotDispatchable). Cite THAT identity for the silent leg; what this node owes is the four witness rows that moved and the controls, which are green by execution. MEASURED on one tree with one claim_batch (PR-lineage binary, sha256 47cdcf6e721a…, NOT a released control, labelled so): an Int at a BARE `T` formal refuses, while the same Int under `FreeMonoid<T>` and under `List<T>` with a source-written `List<String>` settling the parameter produce zero rows. That is the discriminator: a name-keyed hit or a never-made binding would both leave the bare case silent too, and it is not. LANE RULING RECORDED HERE so the next worker does not re-propose it: a helper resolving child slots by name at ONE consumer was DECLINED under gunbc.design_argument::single_authority — it is a second implementation of generic substitution beside substitute_generics_apply and leaves the real bug in place everywhere else. The repair is ONE change to the shared function, measured first (how many call sites' inferred types change across the self-host build and the claim corpus, before/after on a sample, whether v2-bootstrap and self-host still build, the RELEASED binary as the control), and every newly-red site is filed as a latent bug surfacing, never waived.",
    "THE INSTRUMENT CHECK THAT WAS SKIPPED HERE, now a lane rule sourced to this node: before execing ANY leg that tests for a diagnostic, print that diagnostic's literal hit count in the binary about to be execed (`grep -ac RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement <bin>`). Three legs were run here expecting refusals against a `gunbc` whose mtime predated the seed install and whose hit count was 0 — so a clean run was reported as evidence about the ROUTE when it was only evidence about an armless compiler. A green from a binary that cannot produce the refusal is worse than no green, because it reads as a pre-check that passed. The two arm-bearing local binaries (claim_batch, claim_executor) carried 1 hit each; the check costs one grep and belongs BEFORE the leg.",
    "REVIEW TELL: a refusal keyed on `the settled element is not X` is wrong until it also proves the element IS settled and is not a branded refinement of X, and no witness of your own shape can tell you -- only the population can. Measure the rule against the whole population (the regen round typechecks every module; a claim_batch run typechecks only its ENTRY CLOSURE) before believing your green, and treat an unchanged witness table as a failed run.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
